    {
      "id": "bb581f597943c3167acc8b4d9a52007f36a20d0c",
      "short_id": "bb581f59",
      "created_at": "2025-09-27T23:52:09.000-04:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "62d454a445c2be4f9727ba5f6bad304bc278269d"
      ],
      "title": "packet-noe.c: Fix checkapi issue",
      "message": "packet-noe.c: Fix checkapi issue\n\nFor case OPCODE_EVT_BT_BONDING_RESULT, the call to\nproto_tree_add_uint_format_value is inconsistent.\nIt claims the field is 1 byte long,\nextracts 2 bytes (unsigned),\ndisplays it as a signed integer,\nand the HF expects 4 bytes.\n\nNo solution is guaranteed to be perfect, but based on the other fields\nalso being UINTs, it would seem that the %d was\nintended to be %u.\n",
      "author_name": "Moshe Kaplan",
      "author_email": "mosheekaplan@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-09-25T23:54:34.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "Moshe Kaplan",
      "committer_email": "mosheekaplan@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-09-27T23:52:09.000-04:00",
